From f97310348c58c52e2d35cc5bbba4384ccf661e75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:00:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): harden Disk Engram Clock-Pro reader and
 parallelize weight packing

Upstream base: local-inference-lab/vllm 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
with candidate-55's series applied through 0810.

Rationale: Adds Clock-Pro cache shielding and asynchronous stage bounds in the
native Disk Engram reader, hardens partial-init cleanup and idempotent close in
rows.py, speeds up post-load weight packing/warmup across worker ranks, and keeps
DeepseekV41ForCausalLM resolution lazy until instantiation.

Quality implications: None; bit-exact Engram lookups and bounds safety are
verified under host ASan + UBSan and kernel unit tests.

Tests: pytest -q -p deepseek_models tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v41_engram_rows.py
tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v41_postload_startup.py
tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_engram.py (with ASan+UBSan pass on _reader.c).

Upstream status: local candidate-60 patch
